1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

3
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Let's go

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
This world is overflowing with color

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Truth and lies confuse our eyes.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,100
Look carefully with your heart.

7
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:35,079
The truth isn't far away.

8
00:00:35,079 --> 00:00:38,100
Hey you, good or bad, truth or lies?

9
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:41,100
Can't step out of this gray smoke of the heart.

10
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:44,100
Bring all your courage with you.

11
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:47,240
Maybe this can save the world.

12
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:49,420
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

13
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:52,820
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

14
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:55,799
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

15
00:00:55,799 --> 00:00:57,039
Mojo Spy

16
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:14,980
Mystery solved! The mastermind behind the treasure thefts is The Illumin-Eye!

17
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,980
But their true goal is to steal the desperate voices of those who have lost their treasures.

18
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:23,980
They're on the verge of success—will they really get away with it?

19
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,980
Voice Grab Battle

20
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:38,000
BIBO reporting, Captain. Firecracker Long's passionate fireworks were stolen before we arrived. I'm maintaining order at the scene. Next, we plan to...

21
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:43,000
BIBO! Don't use that thing to yell at me, I can hear you fine!

22
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,000
"No manners at all! Shout again and you're fired!"

23
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Such a chaotic scene—doesn't fit the Illumin-Eye's style at all.

24
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:57,000
BIBO, Firecracker Long did all of this himself after finding his precious fireworks missing and completely losing his mind.

25
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,539
Fireworks—

26
00:02:10,539 --> 00:02:13,000
My Passion Fireworks!

27
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,759
Without you, how can I ever make up with my wife?

28
00:02:16,759 --> 00:02:17,780
Oh my god!

29
00:02:17,780 --> 00:02:21,500
But you're this broken up over a firework theft?

30
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:25,439
If you actually saw the fireworks destroyed...

31
00:02:25,439 --> 00:02:28,539
I can't even imagine that.

32
00:02:28,539 --> 00:02:31,139
The Illumin-Eye's next move

33
00:02:31,139 --> 00:02:33,759
should be to destroy the treasure in front of its owner,

34
00:02:33,759 --> 00:02:37,039
then suck away the owner's desperate cry.

35
00:02:37,039 --> 00:02:45,959
The stolen treasures and voices

36
00:02:45,959 --> 00:02:47,659
are people's most precious things.

37
00:02:47,659 --> 00:02:49,739
I must stop the Dark Eye's theft.

38
00:02:49,739 --> 00:02:52,680
Yeah, we really do need to stop them.

39
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:55,899
But you can't do it alone.

40
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:58,620
It'll take everyone working together.

41
00:02:58,620 --> 00:03:00,379
Besides,

42
00:03:00,379 --> 00:03:03,300
we need some tools right now.

43
00:03:03,300 --> 00:03:06,219
I heard screams before I even got out of the car.

44
00:03:06,219 --> 00:03:07,580
And they carried really far.

45
00:03:20,580 --> 00:03:22,300
Mr. Firecracker Long,

46
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:23,640
it's getting late.

47
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:25,159
Time to get up.

48
00:03:32,159 --> 00:03:34,439
Heh heh, you two made us wait a long time.

49
00:03:34,439 --> 00:03:36,740
Just surrender quietly now.

50
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:41,840
So you ugly people are still lurking in this town.

51
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:43,979
Thanks to this pitch-black night,

52
00:03:43,979 --> 00:03:47,879
your ugly faces look a little blurry—

53
00:03:47,879 --> 00:03:50,340
so I don't have to puke on the spot.

54
00:04:07,159 --> 00:04:08,780
Hand over the fireworks.

55
00:04:08,780 --> 00:04:10,400
Split up.

56
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:14,460
Trying to run again?

57
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:27,320
Ugly monster.

58
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:29,439
Don't even think about coming near me.

59
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:51,360
Give the fireworks back to their master.

60
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:54,680
I am their master!

61
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:57,560
No one but me deserves this unmatched work of art.

62
00:04:57,560 --> 00:05:05,680
That guy's real target all along was the bottle of sounds at my waist.

63
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:13,180
Catch!

64
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:31,980
Detective Chen!

65
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:32,519
What?

66
00:05:32,519 --> 00:05:37,060
Didn't expect that woman to be so good at martial arts.

67
00:05:37,060 --> 00:05:38,660
She made off with Firecracker Long.

68
00:05:38,660 --> 00:05:42,960
Dottie, you okay?

69
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:45,300
As long as my fireworks are fine.

70
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:57,540
What are you doing?

71
00:05:57,540 --> 00:05:59,280
Why light it?

72
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:01,500
Light this firework,

73
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:02,879
and once I've collected their screams,

74
00:06:02,879 --> 00:06:04,860
the mission's done.

75
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:05,660
No.

76
00:06:05,660 --> 00:06:07,379
This firework is mine!

77
00:06:15,379 --> 00:06:15,980
Strange...

78
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:18,639
The fireworks festival is still days away

79
00:06:18,639 --> 00:06:21,540
But this firework is truly beautiful

80
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:22,740
You—

81
00:06:22,740 --> 00:06:25,180
How could you, for the sake of a mission,

82
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:27,819
Destroy such a perfect work of art!

83
00:06:27,819 --> 00:06:31,340
You... your heart is uglier than your appearance

84
00:06:31,340 --> 00:06:33,000
Dottie, the beauty of fireworks

85
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,500
Is in the instant they bloom

86
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:36,160
For everyone to see!

87
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:38,680
I won't listen! I won't listen!

88
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:40,379
The fireworks belong to me alone!

89
00:06:40,379 --> 00:06:41,620
I will never

90
00:06:41,620 --> 00:06:43,480
Watch them with those low-class, vulgar people!

91
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:51,900
My fireworks!!!!

92
00:06:51,900 --> 00:06:54,900
Ah!

93
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:03,900
Quick, Locky Qi!

94
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:06,900
Now! Shout the most emotionless lie!

95
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:14,900
I like going to school!!

96
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:18,900
Inhaling this lie...

97
00:07:18,900 --> 00:07:20,900
The whole bottle of heartfelt lament will be nullified!

98
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:23,900
My fireworks...

99
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:30,600
Everyone, shout the most insincere words together!

100
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:38,600
I want to be an ugly freak!

101
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:52,940
I want to work day and night! I want every girl to hate me!

102
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:54,940
Give it back!

103
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:56,540
This is what I paid for love!

104
00:07:56,540 --> 00:07:59,920
Hmph! Your love has already scorned you!

105
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:22,860
I've lost my fireworks of passion...

106
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:26,000
I can't lose my laments too!

107
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:34,600
This person...

108
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:35,600
is no ordinary one.

109
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:36,759
Must be eliminated.

110
00:08:48,899 --> 00:09:00,039
You... why did you save me?

111
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:02,620
Quick! Get out of here!

112
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:16,240
The one I love abandoned me...

113
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:18,860
Yet my enemy saved my life.

114
00:09:18,860 --> 00:09:21,840
Why is this happening?

115
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:23,500
Why?

116
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:30,919
Old sir, there's a package for you.

117
00:09:30,919 --> 00:09:37,600
This...

118
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:37,759
This is...

119
00:09:37,759 --> 00:09:46,220
My fish basin! Hahaha!

120
00:10:07,759 --> 00:10:11,500
[Ending Theme]

121
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:14,679
Saying goodbye to today

122
00:10:14,679 --> 00:10:19,039
Always feels a little lost

123
00:10:19,039 --> 00:10:22,460
Look toward tomorrow

124
00:10:22,460 --> 00:10:26,860
Waving to me from the horizon

125
00:10:26,860 --> 00:10:30,519
Each day, the sun rises and sets

126
00:10:30,519 --> 00:10:34,480
Turning through time, dreaming more

127
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:36,980
Awaiting in life

128
00:10:36,980 --> 00:10:39,539
Every second, every moment

129
00:10:39,539 --> 00:10:46,259
My bright eyes shimmer

130
00:10:46,259 --> 00:10:49,639
A smile that greets the sun

131
00:10:49,639 --> 00:10:52,279
Stepping quietly along

132
00:10:52,279 --> 00:10:54,840
At the screaming crossroads